@startuml
!theme cyborg
skinparam backgroundColor #111827
skinparam defaultFontColor #F3F4F6
skinparam ArrowColor #CBD5E1
title Proposed transaction boundary — local atomicity, external observations
skinparam backgroundColor #111827
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam defaultFontName Arial

rectangle "Current attributable command / expected versions" as IN
rectangle "Evaluated local transaction boundary" {
 rectangle "Owner invariant / revision / uniqueness guards" as G
 rectangle "Owned state mutation" as S
 rectangle "Attributable command result + required pending intent" as P
 G --> S
 S --> P
}
rectangle "Committed durable work discovery" as D
rectangle "Scoped external adapter / native Git / storage effect" as E
rectangle "Guarded attributable observation / reconciliation" as O
IN --> G
P --> D : only committed intent
D --> E : outside local transaction
E --> O : actual confirmed / partial / unknown evidence
legend bottom
 No SQL lock is held while waiting for provider/runner/target work.
 Physical bytes and native refs are not rolled back by SQL; cross-owner reference guards remain explicit.
 Stored result, dispatched request and actual effect are distinct facts.
endlegend
@enduml
